## MER-82: P1.3 red on 5.15.0-181 — root-cause and fix (2026-07-11)

### Failure reproduction

On Lima 5.15.0-181-generic, TestGeneveIngressIdentityPolicyGate_MER21 timed out
after 3 s in AssertAllowed(18080).  Metrics showed ingress FLOWS_ALLOWED=5 but
the TCP connection never completed.

### Root cause

Linux ≥ 5.15.0-181 geneve_rx() enforces:

    if (unlikely(gnvh->opt_len && !(geneve->cfg.info.key.tun_flags &
                                    TUNNEL_OPTIONS_PRESENT)))
        goto drop;

Non-collect_metadata Geneve devices (as required by ADR-0002) never set
TUNNEL_OPTIONS_PRESENT.  Any Geneve packet with opt_len > 0 is silently dropped
by the kernel AFTER tc_ingress returns TC_ACT_OK.  Egress TLV stamping
(tc_egress.c insert_inner_tlv_room) set opt_len=2 on every packet; the ingress
BPF program allowed them but did not strip the TLV before handing back to the
kernel, so geneve_rx() always dropped them.

### Fix (bpf/tc_ingress.c + bpf/include/meridian_consts.h)

Added strip_meridian_tlv() to tc_ingress.c.  It is called on every allowed
Geneve packet (both the enforce_flow TC_ACT_OK path and the non-SYN TCP bypass
path) before returning TC_ACT_OK:

1. Byte-shift inner payload MERIDIAN_GENEVE_OPT_BYTES (8) bytes toward head,
   overwriting the TLV position with inner content.
2. Clear opt_len in Geneve header byte 0.
3. Decrement outer IP total_len by 8 (with BPF_F_RECOMPUTE_CSUM).
4. Decrement outer UDP len by 8.

No bpf_skb_change_tail call: on 5.15.0-181, virtio_net GRO sets
skb->encapsulation before TC ingress fires, making bpf_skb_change_tail return
-ENOTSUPP.  Instead the IP total_len decrement causes ip_rcv() to call
pskb_trim_rcsum() which removes the duplicate 8 tail bytes naturally, without
requiring any tail-trim BPF helper.

